  "solution": "**Given**\n\n**Find the relation**\n\n100 → 1000\n\n100 = 10²\n\n1000 = 10³\n\nSo, the pattern is:\n\nIf a number is a perfect square (n²), it is converted to n³.\n\n**Apply same logic to 64**\n\n64 = 8²\n\nSo, 64 → 8³\n\n= 512\n\nHence, the correct option is **Option 3.**",
